I am taking a little break from work.
I take out my phone to look at a map.
I want to find Eva's address.
She lives completely on the other side of town.
I look closely at the route on the screen.
It is actually quite far away.
Peter comes into the break room to get a cup of coffee.
He looks over my shoulder and asks what I am doing.
"I am going to visit Eva on Friday," I explain.
"Will you cycle there?" he asks.
I think about it for a moment.
I think that I probably will take the bus.
I feel that it simply is too far by bike.
"No, I intend to take the bus," I answer him.
"Then you can also relax on the trip," Peter says with a smile.
He is absolutely right.
I close the app and put the phone back in my pocket.
Now my route is planned.
I am looking forward to a cozy evening.
